# Local Development Environment Variables for the Realtime Worker
# Copy this file to .dev.vars and fill in the values
# IMPORTANT: Never commit .dev.vars to version control

# JWT Secret for verifying WebSocket room tokens (minimum 32 characters)
#
# This MUST match apps/api/.dev.vars JWT_SECRET — the API worker signs the
# room-scoped JWT and the Realtime DurableObject verifies it. If they
# diverge, every WebSocket upgrade fails with "Server configuration error".
#
# Generate a secure secret:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
JWT_SECRET=your-secure-jwt-secret-min-32-chars-long-change-this-value

# Optional: Dedicated secret for guest (customer) realtime tokens. If set,
# guest tokens are signed/verified with this key instead of JWT_SECRET so
# rotating guest credentials does not invalidate staff sessions. Must match
# apps/api/.dev.vars REALTIME_JWT_SECRET.
# REALTIME_JWT_SECRET=your-secure-realtime-jwt-secret-min-32-chars-long
